{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1297690-mage-lore-in-ancient-rome","id":1297690,"title":"Mage Lore in ancient Rome","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-03-18T05:09:50-07:00","id":1297690,"title":"Mage Lore in ancient Rome","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Hello!</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">I'm looking for advice to prepare next adventure of my Vampire Chronicle.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">One of my PCs (an scholar Malkavian) has stablished relations with the Cult of Mercury in 120 BC.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve a basic idea of Mage, their spheres, traditions-technocracy. I read the basic book and some novels. But, I would like to know how mages were organized in Rome, what was their \u201cexplanation\u201d of Magic, what they thought of \u201cbarbarian\u201d mages, etc.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m happy to receive cannon information, or even the name of books I could read to get it; as well, as receiving non-cannon ideas and suggestion on how this could have worked.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Thanks</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11010-ersito","name":"erSito","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-18T05:41:24-07:00","id":1297699,"title":"","content":"The sourcebook Dead Magic has a whole chapter about the mage practices of ancient rome. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It's probably your best bet when it comes to getting a feel of the kind of magic they performed back then - but I don't think there are any books about actual important characters or societies of Mages from that era.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-18T10:57:41-07:00","id":1297767,"title":"","content":"Agreed with Ambrosia. That and the Order Tradition book revised probably are the best resources.<br /> Best bet is to go with he sphere mage system too. The original mystic groups that came up with the Nine Cornerstones in Egypt were gone by then, as I recall, but the Order always hewed closely to those schema even in the Dark Ages. But actual practices are detailed more in Dead Magic. Though fyi - iirc it is a Black Dog boom, so get ready for some possibly unpleasant material...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-18T11:44:54-07:00","id":1297779,"title":"","content":"There is a section about Roman mages in the revised Storytellers Handbook's alternate settings chapter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}